# Checkers
// Play against the computer, against yourself on two boards side by side, or against someone in another tab.
// The rules are in Board.spell, the computer's moves in Computer.spell, and the room a table is kept in, in Checkers.api.spell:
// this file holds the game you see, and what happens after each move.

checkers is an app
	its "opponent" is one of computer, yourself or someone
		-- Who black plays:  the computer, yourself on a second board turned round, or someone in another tab
	"board" is a new board
	"turned board" is a new board with turned = yes
		-- The same game, turned round:  red's view of it
	its "seat" is text
		-- This tab's own name at a table, made up as it opens:  so the table knows which seat it took
	its "table" is a table
		-- The table this tab sits at, against someone in another tab

	when creating it
		set its seat to "tab " && a random number between 1 and 999999
		start a new game on its board
		copy its board onto its turned board

	its "side" is
		-- Which side this tab plays against someone:  the side whose seat it took, else it watches
		"black" if its table exists and the black seat of its table is its seat
		"red" if its table exists and the red seat of its table is its seat
		"nobody" otherwise

	its "message" is
		-- The line above the board:  who's won, or whose move it is
		set game to its board
		set turn to the turn of game as title case
		if game is over and its opponent is computer
			return "You win!" if the winner of game is black otherwise "The computer wins"
		if game is over
			return the winner of game as title case && "wins!"
		if its opponent is computer and the turn of game is red
			return "The computer is thinking…"
		if its opponent is someone and its side is "nobody"
			return "Two other tabs are playing:  New game starts your own"
		if its opponent is someone
			return "Your move" if the turn of game is its side otherwise "Their move"
		if the jumper of game exists
			return turn && "jumps again"
		return turn && "to play"

	group "Who You Play"
	to "play the computer" with title "Computer", icon "desktop"
		-- You play black, the computer red
		selected when its opponent is computer
		set its opponent to computer
		set its table to nothing
		start a new game

	to "play yourself" with title "Yourself", icon "columns"
		-- Black on the first board, red on the second, turned round:  each side moves on its own
		selected when its opponent is yourself
		set its opponent to yourself
		set its table to nothing
		start a new game

	to "play someone" with title "Another tab", icon "users", can't be undone
		-- The table in the room:  the first tab to join plays black, the second red, and any more watch
		selected when its opponent is someone
		set its opponent to someone
		set found to the first table in every table
		if found does not exist
			set found to a new table
			share its board in found
			add found to the tables
		if the black seat of found is ""
			set the black seat of found to its seat
		otherwise if the red seat of found is "" and the black seat of found is not its seat
			set the red seat of found to its seat
		set its table to found
		show found on its board

	group "Game Play"
	to "start a new game" with title "New game", icon "sync alternate", shortcut "N"
		-- Every piece back where it starts, black to move
		start a new game on its board
		copy its board onto its turned board
		if its table exists
			-- a tab that was watching takes black, and red is free for the next tab to join
			if its side is "nobody"
				set the black seat of its table to its seat
				set the red seat of its table to ""
			share its board in its table

	group "Against Someone"
	to "share (a board) in (a table)"
		-- The table takes the board's game, so the other tab sees it
		set the diagram of the table to the diagram of the board
		set the turn of the table to the turn of the board
		set the winner of the table to the winner of the board
		set the jump square of the table to the jump square of the board

	to "show (a table) on (a board)"
		-- The board takes the table's game:  both of this tab's boards show it
		set up the board from the diagram of the table
		set the turn of the board to the turn of the table
		set the winner of the board to the winner of the table
		if the jump square of the table > 0
			set the jumper of the board to the piece of (item (the jump square of the table) of the board)
		copy the board onto the turned board of checkers

	to draw it
		<container>
			<stack>
				<toolbar class="Bar" appearance="pills" shrinkable>
					<text size="big" slot="title" heavy>Checkers</>
					<spacer />
					<action "start a new game" />
					<action "undo" icon-only />
					<action "redo" icon-only />
				</>
				<toolbar class="Opponents" appearance="pills" size="small" aria-label="Who you play">
					<action "play the computer" />
					<action "play yourself" />
					<action "play someone" />
				</>
				<header level="3" class="Message">{its message}</>
				{draw its boards}
			</stack>
		</container>

	to draw its boards
		-- one board against the computer;  against yourself both, side by side;  against someone, your side nearest you
		if its opponent is yourself
			<stack class="Boards" direction="horizontal" wrap>
				<board "board" />
				<board "turned board" />
			</stack>
		otherwise if its opponent is someone and its side is "red"
			<board "turned board" />
		otherwise
			<board "board" />

after moving a piece to a square
	-- Both boards show the move;  then the computer plays, or the other tab hears it
	set board to the board of the square
	if board is the turned board of checkers
		copy board onto the board of checkers
	otherwise
		copy board onto the turned board of checkers
	if the table of checkers exists
		share board in the table of checkers
	if the opponent of checkers is computer and the turn of board is red and board is not over
		pause for 600 msec
		play for the computer on board

a table
	when someone else changes it
		-- the other tab moved:  this tab's boards show it
		if it is the table of checkers
			show it on the board of checkers

a piece
	it "is yours" if
		-- Whether you move it here:  black against the computer;  each board's own side against yourself;  your side against someone
		set board to the board of its square
		if the opponent of checkers is computer
			return its side is black
		if the opponent of checkers is someone
			return its side is the side of checkers
		if the turned of board is yes
			return its side is red
		return its side is black
